Subject: [PATCH] feat(updates): a flagged conversation counts in the sidebar
 number (2080, D716)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

D716 (the founder, 7 Oct): „A flagged conversation counts in the sidebar
number until the owner removes the flag. One number." The tester flagged a
conversation and /updates/count still said followed 0: the count held only
flagged update cards.

GET /updates/count's `followed` now adds the owner's flagged conversations to
the flagged cards. The app's „განახლებები N" is due + followed already, so
nothing changes on its side (FOR_FRONTEND notes it).

DONE WHEN: PUT /threads/:id/follow raises /updates/count's followed by 1, and
DELETE brings it back.

Re-sent after the revert (1b72f5b): the threads half of the count takes its
own parameter, cast to int (pending_updates.user_id is TEXT, threads.user_id
INTEGER; one $1 for both threw „integer = text" on every call). A real-
Postgres test (scripts/ops/malformed.sh) shows the old SQL throwing and the
new count returning 1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
